First cut of the c2w migration.

Design choices:
- Pi WASM is spawned per-prompt (not pooled) via `c2w-net -invoke
  pi-agent.wasm --net=socket`. Bochs boot is ~30s. Process pooling
  / persistent sessions are a follow-up — I chose the simpler shape
  first because pi's --no-session means each prompt reprimes context
  anyway, and I didn't want to conflate two problems.
- Environment variables: c2w-net DOES NOT forward --env flags to
  wasmtime. Worked around this with `wasm-agents/wasmtime-shim`
  (bash) that reads WASMTIME_EXTRA_ENV and injects --env flags before
  the `--` separator. The shim's directory is prepended to PATH
  before spawning c2w-net. Ugly but contained.
- Host reachability: from inside c2w the host is 192.168.127.254
  (c2w-net's gvisor-tap-vsock gateway). NOT 10.0.2.2 (wrong; that's
  QEMU SLIRP which c2w does not use). NOT host.docker.internal.
- Must pass `--net=socket` AFTER the wasm path — it's consumed by
  Bochs (patched fork with wasi-ext socket netdev), not c2w-net.
- Kept the Rust agent loop intact; pi path is opt-in via
  `config.pi.enabled`. Don't delete the Rust loop until pi path has
  been exercised under real load.
- Rust processor's thinking/text streaming: pi sends CUMULATIVE
  partial content per message_update, not incremental deltas. I
  track last seen length per turn and emit only the new suffix to
  the event bus. Different from the LLM-router path which sends real
  deltas.
- MCP server at `/mcp` is a bare-minimum JSON-RPC 2.0 handshake:
  initialize + tools/list + tools/call. Exposes 5 tools (list_tasks,
  create_task, update_task, search_memory, save_memory). No SSE
  upgrade. Full MCP resources/prompts/notifications are follow-up.
  Port 8935 (same as main server) on purpose — keeps one listener.

Known gaps (follow-ups):
- Per-agent long-lived PiProcess pool to avoid 30s boot/prompt.
- Tool-execution events from pi aren't fully wired into the
  conversation message store yet (only streamed as chunks).
- Dispatcher path doesn't stream deltas (just collects final turn).
- No snapshotting yet — c2w filesystem snapshots before writes to
  ~/.pi/ is a separate design.
- wanix-server/ is still started by the main binary; safe to delete
  once pi path replaces all paths.

Validation: manual e2e runs in the session before this commit showed
pi receiving JSONL, reaching llama-server via c2w-net NAT, and
streaming thinking_delta events. No automated test yet — WASM is
1.3GB and boots slowly; a smoke test would need a special mock or a
lighter target.
